<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hertfordshire</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hertfordshire is a county of south-east <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, immediately north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>, with Hertford as its county town. In the late <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a> it was the heartland of the Catuvellauni, and the Roman town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/verulamium">Verulamium</a> stood there beside modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/st-albans">St Albans</a>. After the Roman period it was settled by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxons</a> and divided between Mercia and the East Saxons.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hertfordshire.jpg" alt="Hertfordshire" width="320" height="182" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Peter O'Connor aka anemoneprojectors · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:GOC_Hexton_007_Chilterns_landscape_(24372234911)_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
